What is not here
----------------
No Line 6 firmware, code or data is included or distributed. The build reads
the user's own copy of the official HX Stomp 3.80.0 firmware file and changes
it on the user's computer. The patcher contains the offsets and table layouts
it needs to do that, and checks the input's MD5 first. Firmware built with
it contains Line 6's firmware and should not be redistributed.

No Neural Amp Modeler model files (.nam captures) are included.

Third-party material
--------------------
tools/sharc/sasm.py: the SHARC opcode tables are adapted from
tools/sharc_isa.py of the ghidra-sharc extension
(https://github.com/roblg/ghidra-sharc), licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0 (https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0). That file
transcribes them from the Analog Devices "SHARC Processor Programming
Reference".

Neural Amp Modeler (https://github.com/sdatkinson/neural-amp-modeler,
MIT licence): src/sharc/nam_a2.asm and tools/sharc/nam_lite_kernel.asm are
independent implementations of the A2 WaveNet arithmetic, written from the
model file format; no NeuralAmpModelerCore source is included.

